  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1248 PM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains across East Idaho this weekend, and for\nmuch of next week. Daytime highs climb to near or above records\nfor Sunday and Monday for some locations, with readings reaching\nthe upper 70s to mid 80s for most lower elevations. The only\nwrinkle in the forecast arrives Monday, as several models are\nstill trying to swing some potential convection into the region\nassociated with a weak feature pushing through the flow. The NBM\nis still washing out this potential, so blended in some higher\nPoPs from short term ensembles and capped at isolated. The best\nchances appear to remain across the southern highlands and\nportions of the central mountains, for now, and some of the\nmodels are indicating potential for outflows. So added gusty\nwinds to forecast where thunder was included. QPF looks quite\nlimited, regardless. After the feature shifts through, ridge\nrebounds for dry conditions through the remainder of the week.\nTemperatures cool slightly, but remain warm. Looking ahead to\nnext weekend, the operational GFS and ECMWF are swinging a\ndeeper, more robust trough into the PacNW. Ensemble means carry\na trough through the region next weekend as well, just less\namplified than the operational runs. It could mean a transition\nto cooler temperatures and a return of some precipitation to\nEast Idaho.",
